sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: Nick 2026-11-06, agent strip (b): a release list answers from the deployment history the Gateway records. No Node contact, no agent command (R1).
  %% status: draft
  %% command: instance:release:list
  %% kind: instance.release_list
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  CLI->>GW: instance:release:list 14
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `orbit instance:release:list <instance>`
  %%> - syntax: `instance:release:list <instance> [--json]`
  %%> Input:
  %%> - the numeric Instance ID from `instance:list`
  %%> Who can call it:
  %%> - the `orbit` CLI and the MCP tool send the same request
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - your Node has an access grant to the Node that serves the Instance
  Note over GW: Read the history<br/>retained · selected
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - every deploy and rollback is a run whose terminal result the Gateway records, including the releases the deploy's cleanup removed
  %%> - the retained releases are the ones the history keeps: the first release, `initial`, and after each successful deploy the new selection, the selection before it and the newest other release, three in all
  %%> - the selected release is the one the last deploy or rollback activated
  %%> - it starts no run and contacts no Node
  alt production Instance
    GW-->>CLI: 200 releases<br/>selected release
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the retained release names sorted by name, and the selected one
    %%> - the list is what the history retains, not a scan of the Node: a release removed by hand is still listed, and one kept only because a running process uses it is not
  else development default
    GW-->>CLI: 200 empty list
    %%> Result:
    %%> - a development default deploys in its checkout and has no releases
  else any other Instance
    GW--xCLI: 409<br/>deployment.identity_invalid
    %%> When:
    %%> - the Instance is not an active production Instance with a release layout and a recorded user and home
  end
